/-!
# The ideal-theoretic norm index for a cyclic extension (Lang, ANT VII.4, Theorem 8)

For a finite cyclic extension `L / K` of number fields and an admissible modulus `m` supported on
the ramified primes, the subgroup `P(m)·𝔑(m) ≤ I(m)` generated by the principal ray and the
relative norms has index exactly `[L : K]` in `I(m)`.

This file proves the *lower* bound `[L : K] ≤ [I(m) : P(m)·𝔑(m)]` (the upper bound is
`NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.indexPrincipalRaySupNormRayLe`).  The proof goes through the
idèle-theoretic description of `I(m)/P(m)·𝔑(m)`:

* `NK.CFTLib.ArtinReciprocityIdeal.theta : 𝕀 K → I(m)/P(m)·𝔑(m)` sends an idèle to the class of
  the ideal of `x·b`, where `b` adjusts `x` into the congruence subgroup; its kernel has index
  `[I(m) : P(m)·𝔑(m)]` (`index_rayNorm_eq_ker_index`).
* `theta` kills the principal idèles and the norm idèles; conversely every element of `ker theta`
  lies in `Kˣ·N_{L/K}𝕀 L`.  For the converse, write `z = x·(b) ∈ U_m` with
  `idealOf z = 𝔄 ∈ P(m)·𝔑(m)`, lift `𝔄` to an idèle congruent to `1` modulo `m`, and note that the
  ratio of two idèles of the congruence subgroup with the same ideal lies in the *congruence units*
  `U_m ∩ ker(idealOf)` — which are idèlic norms by admissibility
  (`NK.Existence.congruenceUnits_le_normImage`).
* Hence `[I(m) : P(m)·𝔑(m)] = [C_K : N_{L/K}C_L] = [L : K]`, the last equality being the
  unconditional index theorem for cyclic extensions (`index_eq_finrank_of_isCyclic`).
-/

set_option autoImplicit false
set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false
